	"notes": "Fixed charter destination vocabulary for the OpenYacht protocol: the set list both authorities and consumers validate operating_areas[] slugs against. Entries form a hierarchy via 'parent' (a slug in this list, or null for a top-level region); every entry at every level is a valid destination value — a listing operating across a whole group references the group entry. Groupings follow charter-industry convention rather than strict geography. Names are unique across the list so a consumer that does not recognise a slug can fall back to the name. Versioned like tzdata: consumers vendor a copy and update out-of-band; never fetched at request time. Additions via pull request to this repository. This list is intentionally alias-free: mapping messy source values onto these slugs is an import concern belonging to whichever connector reads that source.",
